WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.287
On this slide, we are focusing on return is different from print.

00:00:04.287 --> 00:00:09.392
Start with the meaning of the idea before worrying about the exact syntax.

00:00:09.392 --> 00:00:15.687
Ask what information is going in, what Python is doing with it, and what result should come out.

00:00:15.687 --> 00:00:21.212
Return sends a value back to the program so later code can store it, combine it, test it,

00:00:21.212 --> 00:00:24.267
or pass it into another function.

00:00:24.267 --> 00:00:26.667
Print only displays a value.

00:00:26.667 --> 00:00:30.362
Think about where this function would appear in a larger project.

00:00:30.362 --> 00:00:37.622
Cleaning one value, calculating one metric, or validating one record can become a reusable function applied

00:00:37.622 --> 00:00:39.886
across many rows, files, or notebooks.
